# GitHub hosts the RENDERED SITE ONLY.
#
# Sources (.qmd, media, _quarto.yml, _extensions, helper scripts) live on this
# machine and are backed up through iCloud. They are deliberately not tracked:
# nothing rebuilds the site from source on push, so the repo only needs what is
# actually served out of _site/.
#
# This is a deny-all list. Everything is ignored unless re-included below, so a
# new top-level directory is ignored automatically and no maintenance is needed
# when a section is added.

*

# The build output. This is what gets deployed.
!_site/
!_site/**

# Repo plumbing and the hourly Firebase pastebin cleanup workflow.
!.gitignore
!.gitattributes
!.github/
!.github/**

# Large lab datasets kept locally for rendering, hosted externally for download.
_site/media/rideshare_2022.csv
_site/media/deep-learning/transfer-learning-mobilenet/dataset/
_site/media/deep-learning/image-segmentation-unet/data/
_site/media/deep-learning/operations-on-word-vectors/data/
_site/media/deep-learning/transformer-network/glove/
_site/media/deep-learning/fine-tuning-a-pretrained-transformer/distilbert-base-uncased/

/.quarto/
**/*.quarto_ipynb

/.luarc.json

# iCloud Drive forks a file when two machines touch it, leaving "name 2.ext"
# copies under _site/. tools/clean_output_conflicts.py deletes them, but it
# refuses to delete anything when even one copy cannot be verified as stale,
# and a jammed cleaner previously let 1,730 of them (84 MB) become stageable.
# These patterns make sure a conflict copy can never reach a commit.
_site/**/* [0-9].*
_site/**/* [0-9]
